# Frontend, brand, and accessibility

- Use server-rendered Django templates, semantic HTML, and progressive enhancement.
- Do not introduce React, Vue, a SPA router, or a component framework without an accepted ADR.
- Exact TheCountyPost colors, fonts, logo rules, spacing, and effects must come from verified evidence recorded in `brand/brand-reference-manifest.json`. Never guess them.
- Consume semantic design tokens. Do not scatter raw brand colors, font families, shadows, radii, or spacing values across components.
- Reuse documented template components/includes with explicit context contracts.
- Escape user content by default. Never use `safe`, `mark_safe`, or raw HTML from users without an approved sanitization boundary and tests.
- Forms need visible labels, required-state communication, field errors, an error summary for multi-step flows, keyboard operation, and preserved entered values after validation failure.
- All interactive controls need visible focus, sufficient target size, and accessible names.
- Do not use color alone to communicate listing, moderation, payment, or validation state.
- Respect reduced motion. Provide useful alt text or empty alt text for decorative images.
- Preserve canonical URL and query-string state in filters, pagination, scope toggle, and sorting.
- Validate public and staff workflows against WCAG 2.2 AA after real brand tokens are supplied.
- Mobile behavior is a first-class acceptance criterion; upload, filtering, and listing creation must not depend on drag-only or hover-only interaction.
